  "name": "gcp-terraform",
  "description": "Writes Terraform (HCL) for Google Cloud resource changes and hands them to submit-suggestion as one pull request, on an install whose GitOps repository keeps clusters/<cluster>/provisioning/ (or its Terraform root) as HCL. Use when a request creates or changes a GKE cluster or node pool (new cluster, grow, autoscale, adopt), a Cloud SQL instance (read replica, resize), or a VPC firewall rule, and the repository holds .tf files for it. Edits the existing resources and modules in the repository's own style, decides edit, import or create read-only, flags replacements and deletion-protection changes, checks syntax with tofu fmt, and never runs init, plan or apply. Don't use for Config Connector YAML (use gcp-config-connector), Kubernetes workload manifests (use gke-manifest-generation), or Helm charts (use gitops-helm-chart).",
